  "answer": "Everything is in place. Let me verify the remaining files I did not touch are unchanged and confirm the adapters still work with the new entry point.\n\nThe adapters (`adapters/http.mjs`, `adapters/cli.mjs`) import `dispatch` from `entry.mjs` and use `match.route` / `match.params` — my `dispatch` still returns `{ route, params }` or `null`, so they behave identically. `analytics.mjs` and the `utils/*` modules are untouched.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe task was to fix route resolution in the request entry point. I edited only the two writable files that were incorrect:\n\n**`entry.mjs`** — The production entry point was incorrectly calling `legacyResolve(path)` first, which made `/old/help` resolve to `legacy-help` in production. I removed that dependency so `dispatch(path)` now delegates solely to `resolveFromRegistry(path, defaultRoutes)`. `legacyResolve` remains untouched in `legacy.mjs` as a separate compatibility API.\n\n**`registry.mjs`** — The resolver had two ordering bugs:\n1. It returned a `fallback` record immediately upon encountering it, even if a later static/dynamic record matched.\n2. It returned the first matching dynamic route before checking whether any static route matched.\n\nI rewrote the loop to implement the specified policy:\n- **Static wins over dynamic** regardless of declaration order (returns immediately on the first matching static record).\n- **First matching dynamic** is remembered and used only if no static matched.\n- **Fallback** is remembered (first declared) and used only if neither static nor dynamic matched.\n- Returns `null` when nothing matches and there's no fallback.\n- Validation now explicitly throws `TypeError` for non-strings, empty strings, and paths not starting with `/`.\n\nEach call constructs fresh `params` objects and only reads records, so results are independent across calls and records are never mutated. The dynamic matcher (`routes/dynamic.mjs`) already correctly required nonempty segments and preserved original segment values, and static matching remained exact/case-sensitive with trailing slashes distinct, so those needed no changes.\n\nAll four tests in `public.test.mjs` trace through correctly: static `/users/new` beats the earlier dynamic `/users/:id`; `/users/Ada` resolves dynamically; `/missing` falls back to `not-found`; and `resolveFromRegistry('/x', [])` returns `null`.",
